# Ansible Automation Platform TLS rotation report

Generated by the `aap_cert_rotate` role, which is **unsupported community
content**: not a Red Hat product, not supported by Red Hat or any Red Hat
employee, and not validated against every platform topology.

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Date | {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }} |
| Install type | {{ aap_cert_rotate_install_type }} |
| Mode | {{ aap_cert_rotate_mode }} |
| Target host | {{ inventory_hostname }} |
| Components | {{ aap_cert_rotate_components | join(', ') }} |
| Installation program run | {{ aap_cert_rotate_run_installer }} |
{% if aap_cert_rotate_install_type in ['containerized', 'rpm'] %}
| Backup directory | {{ aap_cert_rotate_backup_dir }}/{{ aap_cert_rotate_stamp | default('n/a') }} |
{% endif %}

## Certificates served after rotation

| Component | Endpoint | Subject | Issuer | Not after |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
{% for result in aap_cert_rotate_served.results | default([]) %}
| {{ result.item }} | {{ aap_cert_rotate_verify_endpoints[result.item] }} | {{ result.subject.commonName | default('n/a') }} | {{ result.issuer.commonName | default('n/a') }} | {{ result.not_after }} |
{% endfor %}

## Rollback

{% if aap_cert_rotate_install_type == 'containerized' or aap_cert_rotate_install_type == 'rpm' %}
The previous inventory file and certificates are in
`{{ aap_cert_rotate_backup_dir }}/{{ aap_cert_rotate_stamp | default('n/a') }}`
on {{ inventory_hostname }}. Restore the inventory file and the certificate
material, then run the installation program again. Expect a second outage.
{% else %}
The previous TLS secrets are still in the `{{ aap_cert_rotate_k8s_namespace }}`
namespace. Patch `route_tls_secret` back to the previous secret name on the
affected component and let the operator reconcile.
{% endif %}
